134
00:04:22,552 --> 00:04:23,286
Type: sed,

135
00:04:23,286 --> 00:04:23,800
dash I,

136
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:24,241
quote,

137
00:04:24,241 --> 00:04:28,574
S slash timeout equals one slash timeout equals five slash,

138
00:04:28,574 --> 00:04:29,015
quote,

139
00:04:29,015 --> 00:04:30,190
timeout dot P Y.

140
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:31,523
No output,

141
00:04:31,523 --> 00:04:33,872
the file was changed in place.

142
00:04:33,872 --> 00:04:34,890
Run it again.

143
00:04:34,890 --> 00:04:36,377
Type: python three,

144
00:04:36,377 --> 00:04:37,630
timeout dot P Y.

145
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,722
Now it waits long enough,

146
00:04:42,722 --> 00:04:44,326
and prints ok two hundred.

147
00:04:44,326 --> 00:04:46,423
The lesson: always pass a timeout,

148
00:04:46,423 --> 00:04:48,458
pick a number that fits the call,

149
00:04:48,458 --> 00:04:50,247
and handle the Timeout error.

150
00:04:52,297 --> 00:04:52,756
Last,

151
00:04:52,756 --> 00:04:53,767
pagination.

152
00:04:53,767 --> 00:04:57,350
Real APIs return a few items at a time.

153
00:04:57,350 --> 00:04:59,372
Here is pages dot P Y.

154
00:04:59,372 --> 00:05:01,577
Type: cat pages dot P Y.

155
00:05:02,127 --> 00:05:03,696
It starts at page one.

156
00:05:03,696 --> 00:05:05,479
The loop asks for a page,

157
00:05:05,479 --> 00:05:08,332
raises an error for any bad status code,

158
00:05:08,332 --> 00:05:09,687
collects the names,

159
00:05:09,687 --> 00:05:13,824
and follows next page until the server says there is none.

160
00:05:13,824 --> 00:05:14,323
Run it.

161
00:05:14,323 --> 00:05:15,678
Type: python three,

162
00:05:15,678 --> 00:05:16,676
pages dot P Y.

163
00:05:17,226 --> 00:05:17,888
Ten servers,

164
00:05:17,888 --> 00:05:19,265
from four pages of three.

165
00:05:19,265 --> 00:05:22,461
Without the loop you would have seen only the first three,

166
00:05:22,461 --> 00:05:24,885
and your script would silently miss servers.

